Brief Review of Lecture: Control Flow
If / Else = Conditional Behavior
if (x &gt; 0) {
  print("positive")
} else {
  print("not positive")
}
Vectorized If/Else statements are also possible:

x = 0
ifelse(test = x &lt; 0, yes = "is positive :)", no = "is negative :(")



[1] "is negative :("


For loops = repeat over items
for (i in 1:5) {
  print(i^2)
}

Brief Review of Lecture: Functions

function_name &lt;- function(arg1, arg2, ...) {
  # code to execute
  result &lt;- arg1 + arg2  # example operation
  return(result)         # optional, returns result
}

Shortcut Class


A character class with a built-in name, such as \d for any digit.



\d matches any digit;
\D matches anything that isn’t a digit.
\s matches any whitespace (e.g., space, tab, newline);
\S matches anything that isn’t whitespace.
\w matches any “word” character, i.e. letters, numbers, and underscores;
\W matches any “non-word” character.


Note: These all have to be escaped when forming a string to express the pattern.

